        "original_id": "3d69810c-d925-5f57-b879-90d0e6372994",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: I Love Melvin\n- People: Donald O'Connor, Debbie Reynolds, Don Weis, Gloria Jean, Peggy Ryan, Francis the Talking Mule\n- Companies: MGM\n- Topics: American musical comedy films, dancing, Technicolor\n\nFacts:\n- Donald O'Connor was born on August 28, 1925, and he became an American dancer, singer, and actor.\n- Donald O'Connor came to fame in a series of movies in which he co-starred alternately with Gloria Jean, Peggy Ryan, and Francis the Talking Mule.\n- I Love Melvin is a 1953 American Technicolor MGM musical and dancing comedy film.\n- Don Weis directed I Love Melvin.\n- Donald O'Connor and Debbie Reynolds starred in I Love Melvin.\n- Donald O'Connor died on September 27, 2003.",
